_[#698df]","[#b4d78]_#_[#dcf89]"],"description":"Each output neuron will receive a weak signal when SpikerBot sees a person. These usually will not be enough to make an output neuron spike.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775587299558","neuronKeys":["[#3925d]"],"edgeStrings":["[#5ec60]_#_[#3925d]","[#3925d]_#_[#dcf89]","[#3925d]_#_[#698df]","[#3925d]_#_[#8cc43]","[#3925d]_#_[#d4a5d]","[#3925d]_#_[#da143]"],"description":"When Spikerbot detects any object at a medium distance, it will also send weak signals to each output neuron. Again this weak signal may not cause the output neurons to reliably start spiking","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775587371340","neuronKeys":["[#3925d]","[#b4d78]","[#698df]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b4d78]_#_[#698df]","[#3925d]_#_[#698df]","[#5ec60]_#_[#3925d]","[#782a6]_#_[#b4d78]","[#698df]_#_[#eac80]","[#698df]_#_[#16759]"],"description":"If a neuron recevies two weak signals at once, the signals at the input synapse will both add together, causing the output neuron to ocassionally Spike when the inputs line up!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775587405744","neuronKeys":["[#d4a5d]"],"edgeStrings":["[#d4a5d]_#_[#16759]","[#d4a5d]_#_[#eac80]"],"description":"Each output neuron will play a different musical note, and glow a different color.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775587479237","neuronKeys":["[#3925d]","[#b4d78]","[#dcf89]","[#698df]","[#8cc43]","[#d4a5d]","[#da143]"],"edgeStrings":["[#5ec60]_#_[#3925d]","[#3925d]_#_[#dcf89]","[#3925d]_#_[#698df]","[#3925d]_#_[#8cc43]","[#3925d]_#_[#d4a5d]","[#3925d]_#_[#da143]","[#b4d78]_#_[#da143]","[#b4d78]_#_[#d4a5d]","[#b4d78]_#_[#8cc43]","[#b4d78]_#_[#698df]","[#b4d78]_#_[#dcf89]","[#782a6]_#_[#b4d78]","[#698df]_#_[#eac80]","[#698df]_#_[#16759]","[#da143]_#_[#16759]","[#da143]_#_[#eac80]"],"description":"When both inputs are triggered, output neurons will randomely fire as the inputs sync and cause them to fire! You will hear many different tones and see many different lights when a person gets nearby!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775587549043","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#3925d]_#_[#dcf89]","[#b4d78]_#_[#dcf89]"],"description":"Experiment with the synaptic weights connecting to each output neuron. How sensitive can you make the different neurons? Can you build a brain that requires 3 different inputs to make a neuron start to spike?","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Greet Nearby People","description":"Blink and beep when a person is close by!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T16:03:36.453465"}}